{"version":"1.1.0","updated":"2026-09-07","name":"Potato of Life — Full Mapping Roadmap","purpose":"Turn the question 'what can a potato be?' into a complete evidence-disciplined research programme across object properties, spatial structure, geometry, biology, history, symbolism, mythology, philosophy and the wider world graph.","central_question":"What belongs to the potato itself, what has humanity assigned to it, what does Potatoism assign to it, and what structures become visible when these domains are mapped together?","method":"Start with the object. Map properties. Map space. Map relations. Map external meanings. Map Potatoism meanings. Test geometry and scale. Record contradictions. Only then interpret recurring structures.","mapping_stack":[{"order":1,"layer":"object","question":"What is a potato?","work":["botany","anatomy","growth","reproduction","chemistry","nutrition","ecology","agriculture"]},{"order":2,"layer":"properties","question":"What can a potato physically and biologically do?","work":["store","carry nourishment","remain dormant","sprout","divide","regenerate","grow underground","cross soil/air boundary","produce another plant","support a plant cycle"]},{"order":3,"layer":"spatial-potato","question":"How does the potato occupy and transform space?","work":["3D form","length/width/height","volume","surface","curvature","skin","eyes","eye distribution","interior","boundary","centre","axes","sections","wedge","cut face","whole/part","up/down","inward/outward","rootward/sproutward","gravity","light","water","growth trajectory","point clouds","meshes","topology"]},{"order":4,"layer":"relations","question":"What does each property connect to?","work":["root","tuber","eye","skin","wedge","sprout","stem","flower","new tuber","soil","water","sunlight","gravity","human food system"]},{"order":5,"layer":"geometry","question":"What shapes and transformations describe the Potato of Life?","work":["vesica-piscis","mandorla","circle","axis","plane","wedge","